From 2f1c5f4e391981988e856a44cb759dbc57db41e0 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rob Paprocki <hi@rpaprocki.com>
Date: Wed, 30 Sep 2026 00:38:19 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02/30] auth: require login everywhere, re-enable CSRF, token
 or session for /api

- Add LoginRequiredMiddleware (Django >= 5.1; Alpine 3.24 ships 5.2.17).
  All pages, /download and /check_for_file now need a logged-in user.
- Add a login page (accounts/login/) and a POST-only logout button.
- Turn CsrfViewMiddleware back on and put {% csrf_token %} into the
  generator form. The Save/Load Configuration JS neither saves nor
  restores csrfmiddlewaretoken, so a stale token from an old saved config
  cannot overwrite the live one.
- /api/generate and /api/status accept either
  "Authorization: Bearer $RDGEN_API_TOKEN" (compared with
  hmac.compare_digest; no CSRF, since a browser never sends the header
  cross-site) or a logged-in session, which must pass the normal
  X-CSRFToken check. Anything else gets 401 JSON instead of a redirect.
- manage.py rdgen_admin --username U --password-stdin|--generate creates
  or updates the web login. The password is read from stdin, never from
  argv, and is checked against the password validators (minimum length
  12).
- Use reversed URLs ({% url %}) in the templates this touches, so a
  sub-path mount (RDGEN_URL_PREFIX) keeps working.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
